  "question": {
    "text": "The ratio of mass percent of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> of an organic compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If one molecule of the above compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> contains half as much oxygen as required to burn one molecule of compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></msub></math> completely to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The empirical formula of the compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></msub></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
